## Carbon dioxide
component-carbon-dioxide = Carbon dioxide
component-carbon-dioxide-solid-name = Dry ice
component-carbon-dioxide-description-novice = A colourless gas that we breathe out. It is what makes soda water fizzy. Frozen, it is “dry ice”: it does not melt but turns straight into gas.
component-carbon-dioxide-description-school = At normal pressure CO₂ is never liquid: at −78.5 °C solid CO₂ sublimes — turns into gas, skipping the liquid. The gas is heavier than air.
component-carbon-dioxide-safety-school = In large amounts it displaces oxygen. Dry ice causes cold burns — handle it only with gloves.
